      "snippet": "Image type: meme\nVisible text: France passed a law requiring solar panels on\nevery parking lot with more than 80 spaces.\n\nEquals 10 nuclear reactors\nReduces heat island, shades cars\n\nThe US -- 800 million parking spaces. Most of\nthem are uncovered asphalt sitting in direct\nsunlight.\n\nWhy aren't we d",
      "content": "Image type: meme\nVisible text: France passed a law requiring solar panels on\nevery parking lot with more than 80 spaces.\n\nEquals 10 nuclear reactors\nReduces heat island, shades cars\n\nThe US -- 800 million parking spaces. Most of\nthem are uncovered asphalt sitting in direct\nsunlight.\n\nWhy aren't we doing this?\nVisual description: The image is a composite of text at the top and a photograph at the bottom. The text discusses a law about installing solar panels over large parking lots and contrasts this with uncovered parking spaces elsewhere, ending with a rhetorical question. The photograph shows a large parking lot covered by an overhead structure made of metal framing with many solar panels mounted on top. Cars are parked beneath the structure, and the ground markings for parking spaces are visible. The sky is clear and blue in the background.",
